sec.p:
ROC analyses demonstrated AUCs for the Delphi Score of 0.699 (95% CI 0.612–0.787) for ≤ 32+0 weeks and corresponding AUCs of 0.895 (95% CI 0.844–0.946) for the sFlt-1/PlGF-ratio (
Fig. 2
).

Adding the sFlt-1/PlGF-ratio to the Delphi score markedly improved model performance for PE-related deliveries ≤ 32+0 weeks (increase in χ
2
from 16.3 to 72.4, p < 0.001), consistent with a significant likelihood ratio test. The combined model showed good discrimination (AUC 0.891, 95% CI 0.839–0.943), with the sFlt-1/PlGF-ratio remaining the only independent predictor and the Delphi score adding no further predictive value (
Fig. 2
).
